Source release: https://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/maths_past_papers_3[Oxford examination archive release thread], Part C bundle pages 300–304. This is one combined paper covering both courses: section A concerns <Gödel second incompleteness theorem> and <provability logic>, and section B concerns <model theory>. The cover cross-lists Mathematics and Mathematics and Philosophy, both Part C, Thursday 10 June 2010, 2.30pm–5.30pm.

Answer availability checked on 28 October 2026: bounded official Oxford searches by exact year, paper label and both subjects found no advertised exact-paper answers. The https://www.maths.ox.ac.uk/system/files/attachments/PartC%202009-10.pdf[official Part C syllabus for the 2010 examination] confirms the paired course identity. No later-year answer-release policy was assumed applicable.

